From: W1700K local firmware work
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip NPU buffers without an attached provider

Early Airoha provider attachment may fail and leave the device using normal
DMA. The outer NPU initializer still allocates six coherent buffers before
the inner initializer notices the absent provider. Avoid the unused
allocation and a possible -ENOMEM probe failure on that normal-DMA path.

This does not implement rollback after attached-provider initialization
failure.

---

--- a/mt7996/npu.c
+++ b/mt7996/npu.c
@@ -560,6 +560,9 @@ int mt7996_npu_hw_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 {
 	int i, err;
 
+	if (!mt76_npu_device_active(&dev->mt76))
+		return 0;
+
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(dev->npu_txd_addr) % 3);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->npu_txd_addr); i += 3) {
